.TH "XmTabbedStackList" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fBXmTabbedStackListCreate\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListCopy\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListFree\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListInsert\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListAppend\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListRemove\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListModify\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListQuery\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListFind\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListCompare\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleInsert\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleAppend\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleRemove\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleModify\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleQuery\fP,
\fBXmTabAttributesFree\fP \(em functions that manage the list of tabs of a TabBox
.iX "XmTabbedStackList"
.iX "TabBox functions" "XmTabbedStackListCreate"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/TabList\&.h>
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBXmTabbedStackListCreate\fP\fR(\fBvoid\fR);
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBXmTabbedStackListCopy\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmTabbedStackListFree\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR);
.PP
\fBint \fBXmTabbedStackListInsert\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBposition\fR\fR,
\fBXtValueMask \fBmask\fR\fR,
\fBXmTabAttributes \fBattributes\fR\fR);
\fBint \fBXmTabbedStackListAppend\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBXtValueMask \fBmask\fR\fR,
\fBXmTabAttributes \fBattributes\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmTabbedStackListRemove\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBposition\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmTabbedStackListModify\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBposition\fR\fR,
\fBXtValueMask \fBmask\fR\fR,
\fBXmTabAttributes \fBattributes\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmTabbedStackListQuery\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBposition\fR\fR,
\fBXmTabAttributes \fBattributes\fR\fR);
\fBint \fBXmTabbedStackListFind\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBXmString \fBlabel_string\fR\fR);
\fBXmTabResult \fBXmTabbedStackListCompare\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBlist1\fR\fR,
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBlist2\fR\fR);
.PP
\fBint \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleInsert\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBposition\fR\fR,
\fBXmString \fBlabel_string\fR\fR);
\fBint \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleAppend\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBXmString \fBlabel_string\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleRemove\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBXmString \fBlabel_string\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleModify\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBposition\fR\fR,
\fBXmString \fBlabel_string\fR\fR);
\fBXmString \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleQuery\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabbedStackList \fBtab_list\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBposition\fR\fR);
.PP
\fBvoid \fBXmTabAttributesFree\fP\fR(
\fBXmTabAttributes \fBattributes\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
An \fBXmTabbedStackList\fP is an opaque, ordered list of tab
descriptions\&. It is the type of the \fBXmNtabList\fP resource of the
TabBox, the row of tabs that a TabStack displays; a TabBox copies the
list it is given\&. Positions in the list count from 0\&.
.PP
Each tab is described by an \fBXmTabAttributeRec\fP:
.PP
.nf
typedef struct _XmTabAttributeRec {
    XmString          label_string;      /* NULL */
    XmStringDirection string_direction;  /* XmSTRING_DIRECTION_L_TO_R */
    Pixmap            label_pixmap;      /* XmUNSPECIFIED_PIXMAP */
    int               label_alignment;   /* XmALIGNMENT_CENTER */
    XmPixmapPlacement pixmap_placement;  /* XmPIXMAP_RIGHT */
    Pixel             foreground;        /* XmCOLOR_DYNAMIC */
    Pixel             background;        /* XmCOLOR_DYNAMIC */
    Pixmap            background_pixmap; /* XmPIXMAP_DYNAMIC */
    Boolean           sensitive;         /* True */
    XmTabValueMode    value_mode;        /* XmTAB_VALUE_COPY */
} XmTabAttributeRec, *XmTabAttributes;
.fi
.PP
The comments give the values of a new tab\&. \fBXmCOLOR_DYNAMIC\fP and
\fBXmPIXMAP_DYNAMIC\fP make the TabBox use its own colors\&. The
\fImask\fP argument of \fBXmTabbedStackListInsert\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListAppend\fP and \fBXmTabbedStackListModify\fP selects
the fields of \fIattributes\fP that are used, as a combination of
\fBXmTAB_LABEL_STRING\fP, \fBXmTAB_STRING_DIRECTION\fP,
\fBXmTAB_LABEL_PIXMAP\fP, \fBXmTAB_LABEL_ALIGNMENT\fP,
\fBXmTAB_PIXMAP_PLACEMENT\fP, \fBXmTAB_FOREGROUND\fP,
\fBXmTAB_BACKGROUND\fP, \fBXmTAB_BACKGROUND_PIXMAP\fP,
\fBXmTAB_SENSITIVE\fP and \fBXmTAB_VALUE_MODE\fP, or
\fBXmTAB_ALL_FLAGS\fP\&.
.PP
\fIvalue_mode\fP decides who owns \fIlabel_string\fP\&. With
\fBXmTAB_VALUE_COPY\fP the list keeps its own copy of the string and
frees it; with \fBXmTAB_VALUE_SHARE\fP it keeps the caller\&'s string,
which must then stay valid as long as the list uses it and is never
freed by the list\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListCreate\fP returns a new, empty list\&.
\fBXmTabbedStackListCopy\fP returns a copy of \fItab_list\fP (NULL for
NULL) in which every label string is copied and every tab is in
\fBXmTAB_VALUE_COPY\fP mode\&. \fBXmTabbedStackListFree\fP frees a list
and the label strings it owns; NULL is ignored\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListInsert\fP inserts a new tab before \fIposition\fP,
which must be the position of an existing tab, 0, or
\fBXmTAB_LAST_POSITION\fP to add the tab at the end\&. The fields
selected by \fImask\fP are taken from \fIattributes\fP and the others
get the values shown above\&. \fBXmTabbedStackListAppend\fP is
\fBXmTabbedStackListInsert\fP with \fBXmTAB_LAST_POSITION\fP\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListRemove\fP removes the tab at \fIposition\fP, which
must exist, and frees its label string if the list owns it\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListModify\fP changes the fields selected by \fImask\fP
of the tab at \fIposition\fP\&. A tab can be changed from
\fBXmTAB_VALUE_SHARE\fP to \fBXmTAB_VALUE_COPY\fP, which copies
\fIattributes\fP\->\fIlabel_string\fP, but not back\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListQuery\fP fills in all fields of \fIattributes\fP
from the tab at \fIposition\fP and leaves it unchanged if there is no
such tab\&. For a tab in \fBXmTAB_VALUE_COPY\fP mode the returned
label string is a new copy, which \fBXmTabAttributesFree\fP frees;
otherwise it is the shared string\&. \fBXmTabAttributesFree\fP frees
the label string of \fIattributes\fP if its \fIvalue_mode\fP is
\fBXmTAB_VALUE_COPY\fP, but not \fIattributes\fP itself\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListFind\fP returns the position of the first tab
whose label string is equal to \fIlabel_string\fP (as
\fBXmStringCompare\fP(3) decides; two NULL strings are equal)\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListCompare\fP compares two lists\&.
.PP
The \fBSimple\fP functions work on label strings only:
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleInsert\fP and
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleAppend\fP add a tab with the given label
(copied), \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleRemove\fP removes the first tab
with that label, \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleModify\fP changes the label
of the tab at \fIposition\fP, and \fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleQuery\fP
returns a copy of its label\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListInsert\fP, \fBXmTabbedStackListAppend\fP,
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleInsert\fP and
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleAppend\fP return the position of the new tab,
or \fBXmTAB_NOT_FOUND\fP (\-1) if \fItab_list\fP is NULL or
\fIposition\fP is not valid\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListFind\fP returns a position, or
\fBXmTAB_NOT_FOUND\fP if no tab matches\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListSimpleQuery\fP returns a label string that the
caller frees with \fBXmStringFree\fP(3), or NULL if the tab has no
label or does not exist\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListCompare\fP returns \fBXmTAB_CMP_SIZE\fP if the
lists have a different number of tabs or tabs with different labels,
label pixmaps or pixmap placements (changes that can change the size of
the TabBox), \fBXmTAB_CMP_VISUAL\fP if they differ only in the other
attributes except \fIvalue_mode\fP, and \fBXmTAB_CMP_EQUAL\fP
otherwise\&.
.SH "NOTES"
.PP
Earlier releases of \fB<Xm/TabList\&.h>\fP declared
\fBXmTabAttributesFree\fP only under the misspelt name
\fBXmTabAttibutesFree\fP, which the library does not provide; that
name is now a macro for \fBXmTabAttributesFree\fP\&.
.PP
\fBXmTabbedStackListRemove\fP and \fBXmTabbedStackListCompare\fP do
not check all their arguments: do not pass position 0 of an empty list
to the former, or two NULL lists to the latter\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fBXmTabStack\fP(3), \fBXmCreateTabBox\fP(3) and
\fBXmTabBoxGetNumTabs\fP(3)\&.
